drg: eMMC runs of sectors in one command, CMD18/CMD25 + Auto-CMD23 (patch 0913)

drg_emmc.c moved one 512-byte sector per CMD17/CMD24. Boot #18 measured
69-154 KiB/s, and boot #38 took ~25 min to the lock screen: installd,
LaunchServices and SQLite (analyticsd 92 s of kernel time) waiting on it.
A run of sectors is now one CMD18/CMD25 with Auto-CMD23 through one ADMA2
chain, as HMD's kernel drives this controller (sdhci.c, sdhci-msm.c,
sdhci.h): block count in ARGUMENT2, 12-byte 64-bit descriptors (Host
Control 2 = 0x0003, no v4 mode), END on the last data descriptor. One
sector stays CMD17/CMD24; a failed run is stopped with CMD12 (a plain R1b
command, as HMD's sdhci sends it) and redone one sector at a time.
Descriptors take the first 4 KiB of the DMA range. Shim test (same
sequence, scratch region 24 GiB into userdata): 2 MiB written in 14 ms and
read in 13 ms, every word and 11 sectors through CMD17 checked, an odd
100-sector run checked, original restored and checked; one sector at a
time took 753 ms for 2 MiB.

